                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_125\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit changes `onFoodLevelChange` in ArenaListener.java so that, when the arena is running, food level changes are only cancelled if `arena.inArena(p) && lockFoodLevel` \u2014 previously it only checked `lockFoodLevel`, meaning the food-lock affected every player on the server, not just those inside the arena.\n\nTracing this method's history through the candidates: candidate_04 (its original introduction) had `if (!arena.isRunning()) return; if (!(event.getEntity() instanceof Player) || !arena.inArena((Player) event.getEntity())) return; if (lockFoodLevel) event.setCancelled(true);` \u2014 this correctly restricted the effect to players in the arena.\n\ncandidate_125 rewrites this method entirely:\n```\nif (!(event.getEntity() instanceof Player)) return;\nPlayer p = (Player) event.getEntity();\nif (arena.isRunning()) {\n    if (lockFoodLevel) {\n        event.setCancelled(true);\n    }\n} else {\n    // Always locked in lobby/spec\n    if (arena.inLobby(p) || arena.inSpec(p)) {\n        event.setCancelled(true);\n    }\n}\n```\nThis refactor drops the `arena.inArena(p)` guard from the \"arena is running\" branch, so `lockFoodLevel` now cancels the food level change event for ANY player on the server whenever the arena is running \u2014 exactly the bug described in the fix commit message (\"otherwise it affects everyone on the server\").\n\nThe fix commit's diff (`if (lockFoodLevel)` -> `if (arena.inArena(p) && lockFoodLevel)`) applies precisely to the structure introduced in candidate_125, confirming this is the bug-introducing commit. (Note: candidate_128 has an identical diff to the fix commit itself and thus is the actual fix, not the bug-introducing commit \u2014 it was likely included at the boundary of the candidate range.)\n"
                }
              }
            ]
